## Summary of Edits Made

All fact-check fixes have been applied to README.md:

1. **"Don't remember this site"** — Fixed to describe it as a button in the toolbar popup (not right-click menu), showing "Won't remember \<site\>" with Undo for 5 seconds.

2. **Default blocklist categories** — Updated to match the exact section headings from `extension/lib/blocklist.js`: browser pages and private network; sign-in/accounts/one-time codes (including auth paths); email and private messages; password managers; banking/UPI/payments/investing/crypto (including payment paths); health portals; government/tax/ID. Removed invented categories. Added note that the list is editable in Options with "Reset to defaults".

3. **Redaction** — Updated to match `extension/lib/redact.js` exactly: card numbers, API keys/tokens/private keys, SSN-like and Aadhaar-like IDs. Email addresses hidden by default and switchable in Options. Removed phone numbers.

4. **Spec paths** — Fixed to `.kiro/specs/ghost-from-the-past/{requirements,design,tasks}.md`; brief is `docs/BRIEF.md` with 8 sections (verified with grep); 14 tasks (verified with grep).

5. **Hooks** — Described as Kiro agent hooks (not git hooks): `secret-guard` is PreToolUse for shell/write tool calls running `node .kiro/hooks/secret-guard.mjs`; `test-on-save` is PostFileSave running worker vitest on `.ts` files and extension node:test on `.js` files.

6. **Vibe vs spec coding** — Removed "rewritten twice" claim. S1/S2/S4 were spec work; S5/S6/S7 were task-scoped prompts against existing specs (fixes, review, tests, docs).

7. **Contribution statement** — Removed the ~70%/~30% estimates and "heavy lifting" paragraph. Replaced with: "Most application code was written by Hark (an AI agent) while Kiro credits were exhausted; Kiro wrote the steering, specs, hooks and scaffold, and from S5 on reviewed and changed the code." Also changed intro to say Hark is an AI agent (not "pair-programming"/"human review").

8. **Vectorize gap** — Fixed to say the test Worker uses `VECTOR_MODE=d1` because the Cloudflare API token has no Vectorize permission (not "account doesn't have Vectorize enabled"). Removed "automatically falls back" claim; stated exactly: D1 vectors when `VECTOR_MODE=d1` or no `VECTORS` binding.

9. **Setup** — Changed `wrangler.toml` to `wrangler.jsonc`; fixed migrations command to `npx wrangler d1 migrations apply DB --remote` (matches worker/package.json).

10. **MCP configs** — Fixed Claude Desktop to use `command`/`args`/`env` form with `npx mcp-remote`; Claude Code to `claude mcp add --transport http ghost <url>/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer <secret>"`; Kiro CLI to `~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json` (or `.kiro/settings/mcp.json` in workspace) with url + headers.

11. **Tests section** — Worker tests listed as auth, chunk, embed, search, util (no MCP/env); extension tests run with `cd extension && npm test`, 27 tests, jsdom confirmed in package.json; e2e has 21 tests locally, 19 against deployed Worker. Options caption lists real controls.

12. **Free tier section** — Made qualitative ("fits the free tier for personal use") with link to Cloudflare pricing docs; removed specific numbers.
